YouTube is a creative0eating monster, that most marketers underestimate. The true value of YouTibe is unlocked when you have the right processes to support creative diversity, testing, and fatigue management. Shorts tends to drive conversions efficiently, if you have platform-native assets. Android tends to have the worst performance, whether that is due to demographics or a higher percent of bot traffic. TV can capture efficient conversions, but is often difficult to measure. And creative/audience fatigue will swallow all of your learnings and progress, so proactive management is key. 

As you scale spend, you must maintain or increase refresh pacing. Increasing 35%+ without new assets based on proven creative styles will lead to higher CPAs.

If a tactic work, ensure you have the resources to continue iterating on it. Know what creative tactics do and don't work for you plan; have a framework for intentional creative production and testing. Roadmap all new creative launches and phase tests so you gradually feed the machine, rather than overwhelming it at once or leaving it stagnant for a period of time. 
